   601                              <2> 
   602                              <2> ; Each letter is a set of shaded circle-dot BOBs: four cumulative 1-bit
   603                              <2> ; masks per letter (darkest rim first, smallest highlight spot last) are
   604                              <2> ; each flat-filled with a brighter palette shade, layering a cheap sphere
   605                              <2> ; gradient the same way xga_balls shades its ball sprites.
   606                              <2> ; The mask source address is tracked in xdemo_mask_addr: the XGA's map
   607                              <2> ; registers are write-only here, so reading [es:0x14] back after a BitBlt
   608                              <2> ; does not return the address that was written and must not be relied on.
   609                              <2> ; Likewise the destination X/Y (es:0x78/0x7a) and pattern origin
   610                              <2> ; (es:0x74/0x76) auto-advance after a BitBlt completes, so all four must
   611                              <2> ; be rewritten before every single blit - reusing a value set for an
   612                              <2> ; earlier level drew each level one glyph lower, and a stale pattern
   613                              <2> ; origin left over for the next frame broke the octahedron's area fill.
   614                              <2> xdemo_title:
   615 0000059C E80896              <2>     call wait_cp
   616 0000059F 0F82FF00            <2>     jc .done
   617 000005A3 8CC8                <2>     mov ax, cs
   618 000005A5 660FB7C0            <2>     movzx eax, ax
